1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,609
For six lectures you've written records.

2
00:00:03,509 --> 00:00:06,117
Your crew never sees a record.

3
00:00:07,917 --> 00:00:10,526
What they see is this handheld.

4
00:00:10,976 --> 00:00:16,193
Eight apps, and every one of them is made of your words.

5
00:00:17,093 --> 00:00:20,572
Some of those words you chose with care.

6
00:00:21,472 --> 00:00:26,689
And some you typed in a hurry, as a name for yourself.

7
00:00:27,139 --> 00:00:30,183
like the last word on this bar.

8
00:00:31,983 --> 00:00:35,461
Today we read the mission from their side,

9
00:00:35,911 --> 00:00:38,085
and fix what reads badly.

10
00:00:39,285 --> 00:00:42,328
Start with the line that's always there.

11
00:00:42,778 --> 00:00:46,257
Your name, your jobs, and where you stand.

12
00:00:48,057 --> 00:00:49,796
Then the eight apps.

13
00:00:50,696 --> 00:00:54,609
Crew is who's down here, and the way home.

14
00:00:55,509 --> 00:00:59,857
Act is the scene, and it keeps everything you've read.

15
00:01:00,757 --> 00:01:03,800
Look is what's in reach, as buttons.

16
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,874
Pack is what you carry.

17
00:01:07,774 --> 00:01:11,252
Tasks is your own story, and the party's.

18
00:01:12,152 --> 00:01:15,630
Beam, Scan and Fire do what they say.

19
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:20,474
For each one, ask a single question.

20
00:01:20,924 --> 00:01:23,533
Which of my words is this?

21
00:01:24,733 --> 00:01:29,515
A choice with no condition goes to everybody in the scene.

22
00:01:30,415 --> 00:01:35,633
A choice for a job goes to the person with that job.

23
00:01:37,433 --> 00:01:39,172
Now here's the surprise.

24
00:01:39,622 --> 00:01:42,665
The engineer walks up to Marrow alone.

25
00:01:43,565 --> 00:01:47,913
The medic is across the yard, on the landing pad.

26
00:01:48,813 --> 00:01:52,291
And he's offered her answer, marked as covering.

27
00:01:54,091 --> 00:01:57,135
Covering is worked out scene by scene,

28
00:01:57,585 --> 00:02:00,193
from who is standing in it.

29
00:02:01,093 --> 00:02:04,572
So a job is never out of reach.

30
00:02:05,022 --> 00:02:08,065
If only a medic's hands will do,

31
00:02:08,515 --> 00:02:10,689
ask for a skill instead.

32
00:02:11,889 --> 00:02:17,541
That third word on the bar is a mark from your map file.

33
00:02:18,441 --> 00:02:23,659
Any mark somebody can stand on is a word on their screen.

34
00:02:25,459 --> 00:02:27,633
So watch what happens here.

35
00:02:28,533 --> 00:02:32,011
Nobody has asked about the medical kit yet.

36
00:02:32,461 --> 00:02:36,374
And the map has just told her it's there.

37
00:02:38,174 --> 00:02:40,348
So here are two rules.

38
00:02:41,248 --> 00:02:46,030
Name a mark for the place, the way you'd say it.

39
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:49,959
Landing pad. Gully mouth. Foot of the stairs.

40
00:02:50,859 --> 00:02:56,076
And stand a hidden thing on a cell, not on a mark.

41
00:02:57,276 --> 00:03:00,754
An area's title is read after other words.

42
00:03:01,204 --> 00:03:04,248
Go to, in Look. To, in Beam.

43
00:03:05,148 --> 00:03:09,496
So a title that starts with The reads badly twice.

44
00:03:09,946 --> 00:03:13,424
and the fix is to take it off.

45
00:03:15,224 --> 00:03:17,833
Next, the things you pick up.

46
00:03:18,733 --> 00:03:22,211
The transcript says he picked up a toolbox.

47
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,835
The pack says two fuses.

48
00:03:26,635 --> 00:03:28,809
And the key is worse.

49
00:03:29,259 --> 00:03:31,867
The heading says pump house key.

50
00:03:32,317 --> 00:03:35,796
The pack and the door say pump key.

51
00:03:36,696 --> 00:03:41,478
That's the item's key, with its underscore shown as a space.

52
00:03:43,278 --> 00:03:48,061
So make the item's key the same words as the heading.

53
00:03:48,961 --> 00:03:50,700
Three lines name it,

54
00:03:51,150 --> 00:03:53,324
and all three change together.

55
00:03:53,774 --> 00:03:56,383
Lint can't check that for you.

56
00:03:57,583 --> 00:04:00,626
Scan lists everything in sight, scenery too.

57
00:04:01,526 --> 00:04:06,309
With no scan line and no description, it says no reading.

58
00:04:07,209 --> 00:04:10,252
So give your scenery one line each.

59
00:04:10,702 --> 00:04:13,311
It's the cheapest clue you have.

60
00:04:15,111 --> 00:04:17,285
Now open the Tasks app.

61
00:04:18,185 --> 00:04:21,663
On the ship, a quest shows its objective.

62
00:04:22,113 --> 00:04:26,896
Down here it shows a heading, a state, and a lead.

63
00:04:28,696 --> 00:04:33,478
So on the ground the heading has to be the instruction.

64
00:04:34,378 --> 00:04:37,857
The Caretaker's Cough becomes See to Marrow's Cough.

65
00:04:39,057 --> 00:04:42,535
Look at the mission as your helm officer.

66
00:04:43,435 --> 00:04:45,609
No story of her own.

67
00:04:46,059 --> 00:04:50,407
One answer she's covering, and a panel that refuses her.

68
00:04:52,207 --> 00:04:56,554
Two of your five crew have come down to watch.

69
00:04:57,454 --> 00:05:03,107
So give each of them a story, and one answer that finishes it.

70
00:05:03,557 --> 00:05:07,904
You know every word of this from the fifth lecture.

71
00:05:09,704 --> 00:05:12,748
Lint warns that nothing sends the signals,

72
00:05:13,198 --> 00:05:16,676
and then the two answers put that right.

73
00:05:17,876 --> 00:05:20,050
Somebody stays on the bridge.

74
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,239
Here's everything they get.

75
00:05:24,039 --> 00:05:26,648
A list of who went down.

76
00:05:27,548 --> 00:05:31,026
The shared quests, as they start and finish.

77
00:05:31,926 --> 00:05:34,100
And one line in Messages,

78
00:05:34,550 --> 00:05:38,028
when somebody on the ground presses Report in.

79
00:05:39,828 --> 00:05:42,872
No scene line ever reaches the bridge.

80
00:05:43,772 --> 00:05:47,250
So the shared quests are its only window.

81
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:49,874
Remember that for the capstone.

82
00:05:51,674 --> 00:05:56,022
For the exercise, play it to read, not to win.

83
00:05:56,922 --> 00:06:00,400
Write down every word that makes you wince,

84
00:06:00,850 --> 00:06:03,893
and then go and fix each one.

85
00:06:05,693 --> 00:06:09,172
Next time, we put a clock on it.
